s elsewhere (e.g., health and social care) or create future demand if community capacity erodes at a time of budget pressure.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"MTFS App 2 Savings Proposals 2027-30 (@ 20-08-2026)","paper_url":"https://burnley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51892/51892.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"35% of proposed savings (\u00a372,840) deferred pending Boundary Commission review, with implementation timing uncertain","lead":"Deferred savings create budget delivery risk. If the boundary review outcomes or timelines differ from assumptions, the council's savings targets become unachievable.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"MTFS App 2 Savings Proposals 2027-30 (@ 20-08-2026)","paper_url":"https://burnley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51892/51892.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Budget gap of \u00a31,841,808 identified with proposed savings of only \u00a3206,491, leaving \u00a31,585,317 unfunded across the three-year MTFS","lead":"A large unfunded deficit indicates either the MTFS is incomplete or the council will need to draw on reserves, defer capital, or seek additional borrowing to balance the budget.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"MTFS App 2 Savings Proposals 2027-30 (@ 20-08-2026)","paper_url":"https://burnley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51892/51892.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"MTFS App 2 Savings Proposals 2027-30 (@ 20-08-2026)","paper_url":"https://burnley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51892/51892.pdf","headline":"Citizens Advice Bureau and Council for Voluntary Service facing significant grant cuts, with CVS proposal explicitly noting adverse health impacts","detail":"CAB grant cut from \u00a351,000 to \u00a345,000 (part of a decade-long reduction that has 'nearly halved' the grant), and CVS cut from \u00a321,500 to \u00a310,000. The CVS proposal explicitly warns that reductions will cause 'reduction in capacity in the local VCFS' leading to 'adverse health impacts as volunteering has proven health benefits.' CAB has also been 'unable to provide user data for its service in Burnley.'","category":"other","matters":"Cuts to social infrastructure and voluntary sector support may shift costs elsewhere (e.g., health and social care) or create future demand if community capacity erodes at a time of budget pressure.","figures":"CAB grant nearly halved over the last decade; CVS cut from \u00a321,500 to \u00a310,000; CAB grant being reduced to \u00a345,000","quote":"This in turn could have adverse health impacts as volunteering has proven health benefits.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"MTFS App 2 Savings Proposals 2027-30 (@ 20-08-2026)","paper_url":"https://burnley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51892/51892.pdf","headline":"35% of proposed savings (\u00a372,840) deferred pending Boundary Commission review, with implementation timing uncertain","detail":"Two major proposals totaling \u00a372,840\u2014reduction of councillor numbers from 45 to 33 (saving \u00a342,840) and move to all-out elections (\u00a330,000)\u2014are both deferred pending the Boundary Commission review and legislative approval. The council has requested 2027 implementation but both have been moved to future years, making their delivery dependent on external decisions.","category":"governance","matters":"Deferred savings create budget delivery risk. If the boundary review outcomes or timelines differ from assumptions, the council's savings targets become unachievable.","figures":"\u00a342,840 deferred for ward review; \u00a330,000 for all-out elections; councillor reduction from 45 to 33; \u00a33,570 per annum councillor allowance; \u00a36,500 cost per by-election","quote":"Potential reduction in the number of Councillors from 45 to 33. This is subject to a Boundary Commission review and may change. The saving is based upon saving 12 x member allowances - currently \u00a33,570 per annum.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"MTFS App 2 Savings Proposals 2027-30 (@ 20-08-2026)","paper_url":"https://burnley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51892/51892.pdf","headline":"Budget gap of \u00a31,841,808 identified with proposed savings of only \u00a3206,491, leaving \u00a31,585,317 unfunded across the three-year MTFS","detail":"The council identifies a total budget gap of \u00a31.84m over 2027-30 but proposes savings of only \u00a3206k. Even after these savings, \u00a31.59m (86% of the identified gap) remains unfunded. The document provides no explanation of how this large remaining deficit will be addressed.","category":"savings","matters":"A large unfunded deficit indicates either the MTFS is incomplete or the council will need to draw on reserves, defer capital, or seek additional borrowing to balance the budget.","figures":"\u00a31,841,808 budget gap identified; \u00a3206,491 total savings proposed; \u00a31,585,317 adjusted budget gap remaining","quote":"Adjusted Budget gap after savings proposals\u00a31,585,317 \u00a3497,652 \u00a3727,089 \u00a3360,575","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Revenue Monitoring Q1 2026-27 App 2","paper_url":"https://burnley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51883/51883.pdf","headline":"Pension Strain reserve entirely depleted through inter-reserve transfers","detail":"The Pension Strain reserve, which stood at \u00a31,113k, was completely transferred to other reserves through the budget movements approved in March 2026, resulting in a zero balance. This reserve is held to cover early termination and redundancy-related pension liabilities.","category":"people","matters":"Completely depleting this reserve indicates the council anticipated significant and specific pension costs that it fully provisioned for. With zero balance remaining, the council has no buffer if additional unexpected pension liabilities arise later in the year.","figures":"Pension Strain reserve: \u00a31,113k opening, entirely transferred out, \u00a30k closing","quote":"Pension Strain 1,113 (1,113) - - -","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Revenue Monitoring Q1 2026-27 App 2","paper_url":"https://burnley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51883/51883.pdf","headline":"Business Rates Retention Volatility reserve drawn by \u00a32m in Q1","detail":"The Business Rates Retention Volatility reserve, which held \u00a32,763k at the start of 2026-27, was drawn down by \u00a32,000k in Q1, leaving \u00a3763k. This reserve exists specifically to smooth income fluctuations from business rates.","category":"income","matters":"Business rates are volatile and unpredictable; drawing 72% of this volatility buffer in the first quarter signals immediate business rates income pressure. This depletes the council's cushion for managing the inherent volatility of this income source for the remainder of the year.","figures":"Business Rates Retention Volatility: \u00a32,763k opening, (\u00a32,000k) Q1 movement, \u00a3763k closing","quote":"Business Rates Retention Volatility 2,763 - - (2,000) 763","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-16"},"name":"Burnley","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Citizens Advice Bureau and Council for Voluntary Service facing significant grant cuts, with CVS proposal explicitly noting adverse health impacts","lead":"Cuts to social infrastructure and voluntary sector support may shift costs elsewhere (e.g., health and social care) or create future demand if community capacity erodes at a time of budget pressure.","also":["66 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Full Council on 2026-09-23","n_findings":67,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"MTFS App 2 Savings Proposals 2027-30 (@ 20-08-2026)","top_paper_url":"https://burnley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51892/51892.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":147,"news_drafts_total":3}}